WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.930
Speaker 1: One of the things I've been saying
during this pseudo scandal involving Republican

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.529
Congresswoman Liz Cheney is that we should
not forget who Liz Cheney is.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:12.460
Liz Cheney is nothing more than a Republican
with whom I disagree on basically every relevant

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.250
policy question.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.900
And she happens to correctly believe that
Joe Biden won the election and it shouldn't

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.690
be a controversial belief that is it.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:24.391
And it's been disappointing to see even some
on the supposed left talk about we should

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:29.439
stand with Liz Cheney, stand with her for
what Republicans want a stripper of her leadership

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:30.460
role as they did.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.029
Let them figure it out.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:34.579
I don't care to defend Liz Cheney one way
or the other.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:35.579
Sure.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:36.579
It's funny.

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:39.899
It's curious to see the incredible double
standard where the right claims to oppose

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:41.690
so-called cancelation.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.210
And yet they canceled Liz Cheney's leadership
position for something that should be uncontroversial,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.789
which is Trump.

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:49.390
Trump really lost the election.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.390
That's it.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.840
But I have no interest in defending Liz Cheney
or standing with Liz Cheney.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.890
And case in point, she was interviewed by
Fox News's Bret Baier late last week.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.640
And on one issue, the 2020 election results,
she did a really great thing.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.980
She told Fox News host Bret Bair.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.410
Your network has to tell the truth about this
issue.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.580
Bret Bair didn't like it.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.000
Lots of people did that.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
A Republican went on FOX News and said, you
need to tell the truth about the election.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Let's take a look.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.310
Speaker 3: And then I continued to say it,
though, when I say in principle, it's because

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.830
people of Winogrand
Speaker 2: who are electing a congressperson

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.290
to fight for them and to fight against the
Biden agenda.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:33.370
Why wouldn't they say, is this the person
that's going to get it done?

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.840
Because your colleagues
Speaker 3: are.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.490
I'm going to I'm going to answer the question.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:43.350
We all have an obligation and I would say
Fox News, especially, especially Fox News,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.430
has a particular obligation to make sure people
know the election wasn't stolen.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.870
Fox News, FOX News.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.380
Bret, I'm going to answer your question.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.580
Fox News needs to make sure that if you're
FOX News, you have to make sure that the American

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:57.580
people.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.110
Bret, you're doing the interview.

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:00.380
I'm answering the question, Congressman.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:05.490
We need to make sure that the American people
recognize and understand that the election

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:10.110
wasn't stolen, that we shouldn't perpetuate
the big lie and that there's real danger.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.060
You know, I've worked in countries around
the world.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.670
Speaker 1: OK, so it's great, right?

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.670
I mean, I agree.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.920
That's great seeing a Republican do that on
Fox News.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:17.950
That's great stuff.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:23.530
But then and this is the bigger point, Bret
Bair asks Liz Cheney, did you vote for Joe

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:24.530
Biden?

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:25.530
She's so anti Trump.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.670
Did you vote for Joe Biden?

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:31.610
And she says not only did she not vote for
Joe Biden against Trump, she would never vote

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.580
for any Democrat, period.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:34.880
Doesn't matter who it is.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:35.880
Take a look.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.340
Speaker 3: And we are going to abide by the
rule of law.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:44.150
Speaker 2: Do you believe that America is
better off with President Biden than President

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.150
Trump?

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.190
Speaker 3: I believe that President Trump's
policies, which I supported 93 percent of

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.360
the time, were much better for America.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.160
Now, that isn't the issue, though.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.770
The issue is whether or not we abide by the
rule of law.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:03:01.250
Did you for what I did not whether and I would
not and I would not vote for a Democrat ever.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.730
Speaker 1: Do not forget who Liz Cheney is.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:10.240
Her depraved, immoral party of which she's
a proud member.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.430
Did her wrong.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.040
OK, they can figure it out.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.280
We're not standing with her or them.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:22.320
She may be anti the former guy, anti Trump,
but she's still a right winger and a radical

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.320
one.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.480
Is that as left as I am?

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.200
I would never make a proactive, preemptive
blanket statement.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.430
Like I would never vote for a Republican.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:38.280
If you give me a specific race and the Republican
is better than the Democratic option, then

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.630
I'd vote for the Republican.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:40.630
It's that simple.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:46.430
The fact that she's making such a statement
with no caveats about the quality of the Republican

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:50.270
and the quality of the Democrat really shows
us what we should have already known, which

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:56.810
is Liz Cheney is no different than the Trump
McCarthy wing of the party with some slightly

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:57.810
different beliefs.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.130
But remember, she voted with Trump.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.130
What was it?

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.480
Ninety two percent of the time, something
like that.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.090
She's burning a bridge that's already on fire.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.410
And we shouldn't see it as a particularly
brave move or anything like it.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:10.790
I don't take sides in the Trump and Civil
War.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.240
It's bad for them.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.240
Let the war rage.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.009
I have no interest in defending anybody on
either side of it.

00:04:16.009 --> 00:04:20.669
Mitt Romney, anti Trump Republican, didn't
vote for Trump, marched with Black Lives Matter.

00:04:20.669 --> 00:04:21.820
OK, he was asked.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.750
OK, Mr. Mr. Romney, sir, now that Biden's
president, what next?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:30.210
And he said his priority is preventing tax
increases and preventing socialism.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.860
These are not our friends, and it's important
not to be tricked into thinking they are.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:39.620
Liz Cheney has been silent on the voter suppression
bills that have been spreading nationally.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.840
She's doing nothing to speak out against it.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.650
She just doesn't believe that Trump won.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.960
She doesn't believe that lie.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.360
It's not heroic.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:53.820
And this is why Liz Cheney shouldn't be lionized
just for being one Republican willing to tell

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.470
one simple truth.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.340
At the end of the day, she doesn't really
want anything to change.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.129
And you heard it from her, she would never
vote for any Democrat, period

